// Hand-maintained companion to the generated a2a_pb.bal. NOT generated by
// `bal grpc` -- see a2a/proto/PROVENANCE.md and the gRPC transport binding
// design doc's "Finding 2" / "Known limitation 3" for why this file exists.
//
// Why: `ballerina/grpc`'s ServiceDefinition.getFileDescriptor() resolves a
// root FileDescriptorProto's `dependency` entries ONLY from the descriptor
// map handed to `grpc:Client.initStub`, then calls
// `FileDescriptor.buildFrom(proto, deps, /*allowUnknownDependencies=*/true)`.
// Any dependency missing from that map therefore resolves to a protobuf
// *placeholder* descriptor whose file is named "<Type>.placeholder.proto".
// At (de)serialization time `grpc.Message.getDescriptor()` detects the
// placeholder and re-resolves it by message name through
// `StandardDescriptorBuilder.getFileDescriptorFromMessageName()`, whose table
// covers google.protobuf.{Any,Empty,Timestamp,Duration,Struct} and the nine
// wrappers -- but NOT google.protobuf.Value / ListValue / NullValue. So a
// field typed `google.protobuf.Struct` survives the placeholder round trip
// (which is why `metadata`/`params`/`header` always worked) while
// `Part.data`, typed `google.protobuf.Value`, hit a null FileDescriptor and
// failed with
//   "Failed to frame message: Cannot invoke
//    Descriptors$FileDescriptor.findMessageTypeByName(String) because
//    fileDescriptor is null".
//
// Fix: supply google/protobuf/struct.proto's own FileDescriptorProto in the
// descriptor map so the dependency resolves for real and Value/ListValue/
// NullValue are never placeholders. `grpc.Message` already implements the
// full google.protobuf.Value <-> Ballerina `anydata` mapping (see its
// GOOGLE_PROTOBUF_VALUE_STRUCT_VALUE / GOOGLE_PROTOBUF_VALUE_LIST_VALUE /
// GOOGLE_PROTOBUF_LISTVALUE_VALUES branches) -- that machinery was simply
// unreachable while the descriptor was a placeholder.
//
// Provenance of GOOGLE_PROTOBUF_STRUCT_DESC: the uppercase hex encoding of
// the serialized FileDescriptorProto for google/protobuf/struct.proto, as
// produced by
//   protoc --descriptor_set_out=struct.fds google/protobuf/struct.proto
// (protoc 3.21.7 -- the exact protoc `bal grpc` downloads and uses; the
// struct.proto input is the copy bundled inside grpc-native-1.14.7.jar) and
// then stripping the one-file FileDescriptorSet's leading `0A <varint len>`
// tag. This descriptor is a frozen, versionless protobuf well-known type;
// it does not track the A2A spec and does not need regenerating when
// a2a.proto moves. Verified by a2a/tests/grpc_wire_test.bal.
public const string GOOGLE_PROTOBUF_STRUCT_DESC = "";

# Dependency descriptors handed to `grpc:Client.initStub` alongside
# `A2A_DESC`, keyed by the exact `dependency` file names declared in
# a2a.proto's FileDescriptorProto.
#
# Only google/protobuf/struct.proto is listed. a2a.proto also depends on
# google/protobuf/empty.proto and google/protobuf/timestamp.proto, but both
# of those ARE covered by `StandardDescriptorBuilder`'s message-name table,
# so their placeholder descriptors are re-resolved correctly and adding them
# here would change working behaviour for no benefit.
public const map<string> A2A_DESCRIPTOR_MAP = {"google/protobuf/struct.proto": GOOGLE_PROTOBUF_STRUCT_DESC};
